            "body": "### Summary\n\nThis PR delivers a mobile-focused UX upgrade for ttyd and includes the latest related fixes in the same series.\n\nCommits included:\n- fix(html): handle lineHeight layout recalculation\n- fix(html): stabilize iOS keyboard viewport and background\n- feat(html): add mobile virtual keyboard and touch optimizations for iOS/Android\n\n### Features\n\n#### Mobile Virtual Keyboard\n- Add a draggable floating keyboard panel for touch devices.\n- Support modifier keys with active-state feedback.\n- Provide configurable layouts for dynamic function/navigation keys.\n- Support hold-to-repeat behavior with configurable delay and intervals.\n\n#### Touch Interaction Enhancements\n- Improve multi-tap selection workflow.\n- Add modifier-assisted selection flows.\n- Improve on-screen interaction ergonomics for touch-first usage.\n\n#### Clipboard UX\n- Add/improve copy and paste actions through the mobile keyboard controls.\n- Keep clipboard action behavior integrated with current terminal selection state.\n\n### Technical Details\n\n#### Client Options\n```ts\nmobileTapSelectionEnabled?: boolean;\nmobileKeyboardEnabled?: boolean;\nmobileKeyboardOpacity?: number;\nmobileKeyboardScale?: number;\nmobileKeyboardLayouts?: DynamicKeyId[][];\nmobileKeyboardHoldDelayMs?: number;\nmobileKeyboardHoldIntervalMs?: number;\nmobileKeyboardHoldWheelIntervalMs?: number;\n```\n\n#### Main Files\n- `html/src/components/terminal/xterm/mobile-keyboard.ts` (new)\n- `html/src/components/terminal/xterm/index.ts` (integration/lifecycle/options/events)\n- `html/src/components/app.tsx` (defaults)\n- `html/src/style/index.scss` (mobile panel/touch styles)\n- `man/ttyd.man.md` (source markdown docs)\n- `man/ttyd.1` (generated from `man/ttyd.man.md`)\n- `src/html.h` (generated frontend bundle header)\n\n### Changes\n\n- **Added**: `html/src/components/terminal/xterm/mobile-keyboard.ts`\n- **Modified**: `html/src/components/terminal/xterm/index.ts`\n- **Modified**: `html/src/components/app.tsx`\n- **Modified**: `html/src/style/index.scss`\n- **Modified**: `man/ttyd.man.md`\n- **Modified (generated)**: `man/ttyd.1`\n- **Modified (generated)**: `src/html.h`\n\n### Testing\n\n#### Automated\n```bash\ncd html\nyarn run check\nyarn run build\n```\n\n#### Manual Checklist\n- [x] iOS Safari/Chrome: mobile keyboard panel renders and can be dragged.\n- [x] iOS Safari/Chrome: virtual keys send expected input.\n- [x] iOS Safari/Chrome: modifier key toggle feedback works.\n- [x] iOS Safari/Chrome: copy/paste actions work from the mobile panel.\n- [x] iOS Safari/Chrome: hold-repeat behavior works with configured timing.\n- [x] iOS Safari/Chrome: multi-tap selection behavior works as expected.\n- [x] Desktop behavior remains unchanged.\n- [ ] Android device testing (not available in current environment).\n\n### Compatibility\n\n- Mobile enhancements are touch-device oriented and configurable via client options.\n- Existing desktop interaction model remains unchanged.\n- No breaking CLI/API changes introduced.\n\n### Additional changes in this update\n\nThis push adds two focused improvements to the mobile virtual keyboard:\n\n1. **Configurable custom keys (`mobileKeyboardCustomKeys`)**\n   - Supports defining custom dynamic keys as `{ id, label, combo }`.\n   - `combo` is a sequence of key steps (e.g. `[\"Ctrl+b\", \"[\"]`).\n   - `id` validation is enforced (`^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,31}$`) and reserved/unsafe ids are rejected.\n   - Custom keys can be referenced directly inside `mobileKeyboardLayouts`.\n\n2. **Per-key auto layout switch (`mobileKeyboardLayouts` item object form)**\n   - Each layout item can now be either a string key id or an object: `{ \"key\": \"...\", \"page\": n }`.\n   - When `page` is set, pressing that key dispatches the key action first, then switches to the target layout page.\n   - `page` is 1-based; invalid/non-integer/out-of-range values are ignored for switching (key dispatch still works).\n\n### Tests added/updated\n\n- `mobile-keyboard-layout-switch.test.js`\n- `xterm-mobile-keyboard-config.test.js`\n- `mobile-keyboard.test.js`\n- `xterm-mobile-keyboard-action.test.js`\n",
